  {%- when 'terms' -%}
    <p class="sts-legal__eyebrow">Information</p>
    <h1 class="sts-legal__heading">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
    <p class="sts-legal__updated">Last updated 2 November 2026</p>
    <p>These terms apply to visits, bookings, and purchases at St Swithins Wine Shippers, 11–12 St Swithin’s Lane, London EC4N 8AL.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>St Swithins Wine Shippers is a wine shop and tasting terrace in the City of London. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:info@stswithinswineshippers.com">info@stswithinswineshippers.com</a> or +44 20 7621 9972.</p>

    <h2>Age</h2>
    <p>You must be 18 or over to buy or drink alcohol. We may ask for proof of age. We will refuse service where we cannot confirm that you are 18 or over.</p>

    <h2>Visiting the shop and terrace</h2>
    <p>We are open Monday to Friday, 12pm–10pm, unless we say otherwise. Tables on the tasting terrace can be reserved. Walk-ins are welcome when we have space. We may refuse or end service if behaviour puts other guests or our team at risk.</p>

    <h2>Bookings</h2>
    <p>Reservations are made through our booking form or by email or telephone. Please tell us about group size, allergies, and any other needs when you book. If you cannot come, let us know as soon as you can so we can offer the table to someone else.</p>
    <p>Larger groups, tastings, and private events are arranged with us directly. Those bookings may have their own deposit or cancellation terms, which we will confirm in writing.</p>

    <h2>Food and wine</h2>
    <p>Terrace food is prepared to order and may contain allergens. Please speak to the team before you order. Wine by the glass is served from Enomatic and Coravin systems; availability changes.</p>

    <h2>Purchases</h2>
    <p>Bottles, gifts, and other goods bought in the shop are paid for in store. Title passes on payment. Please check your items before you leave. We cannot accept the return of alcohol that has been opened, unless it is faulty.</p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or for fraud. We are not responsible for loss that was not foreseeable, or for events outside our reasonable control.</p>

    <h2>Law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales. The courts of England and Wales have exclusive jurisdiction.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The version on this page is the current one.</p>

  {%- when 'privacy' -%}
    <p class="sts-legal__eyebrow">Information</p>
    <h1 class="sts-legal__heading">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="sts-legal__updated">Last updated 2 November 2026</p>
    <p>This policy explains how St Swithins Wine Shippers collects and uses personal information. We are based at 11–12 St Swithin’s Lane, London EC4N 8AL.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>We may collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Name, email address, and telephone number when you contact us, join the newsletter, or book a table</li>
      <li>Booking details such as date, time, and group size</li>
      <li>Messages you send through the contact form</li>
      <li>Technical information such as IP address and browser type when you use this website</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not ask for payment card details through this website.</p>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>We use this information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Reply to enquiries and manage reservations</li>
      <li>Send newsletter emails if you have asked us to</li>
      <li>Run and improve this website</li>
      <li>Meet legal duties that apply to a licensed premises</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Our legal bases under UK GDPR are typically your consent (newsletter and optional cookies), performance of a contract or steps you ask us to take (bookings and enquiries), and legitimate interests (running the website and the venue).</p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We share information only where needed:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Shopify, which hosts this website</li>
      <li>ResDiary, which powers table bookings</li>
      <li>Email and hosting providers who process data for us</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your information.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Contact messages and booking records are kept only as long as we need them to deal with your request and our records, then deleted or anonymised. You can unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us for a copy of your information, to correct it, to delete it, or to restrict or object to how we use it. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:info@stswithinswineshippers.com">info@stswithinswineshippers.com</a> or write to us at the address above.</p>

  {%- when 'cookies' -%}
    <p class="sts-legal__eyebrow">Information</p>
    <h1 class="sts-legal__heading">Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="sts-legal__updated">Last updated 2 November 2026</p>
    <p>This website uses cookies and similar technologies. This policy explains what they are and how we use them.</p>

    <h2>What cookies are</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small files stored on your device. They help a site remember your visit, keep a page working, or understand how the site is used.</p>

    <h2>Cookies we use</h2>
    <p><strong>Strictly necessary.</strong> These cookies are needed for the site to work. They include session cookies from Shopify, which hosts the shop, and cookies that remember cookie choices if a banner is shown. The site cannot function properly without these.</p>
    <p><strong>Functional.</strong> These remember preferences such as language or region where those tools are enabled.</p>
    <p><strong>Analytics.</strong> Shopify may set analytics cookies so we can see, in aggregate, which pages are used. We use this to improve the site, not to identify you.</p>
    <p><strong>Third parties on some pages.</strong> The Visit page loads a ResDiary booking widget, which may set its own cookies. Social links take you to Instagram, Facebook, or X, which have their own policies.</p>

    <h2>How to control cookies</h2>
    <p>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking strictly necessary cookies may stop parts of the site from working. You can also use browser controls and, where shown, our cookie banner to refuse non-essential cookies.</p>

    <h2>More information</h2>
    <p>See our <a href="/pages/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for how we use personal information. Questions: <a href="mailto:info@stswithinswineshippers.com">info@stswithinswineshippers.com</a>.</p>
{%- endcase -%}
